        "answer": {
          "short": "$y$: $1,\\ 3,\\ 5,\\ 7,\\ 9$ for $x=0,1,2,3,4$, respectively.",
          "worked": "The gradient is $2$, so each increase of $1$ in $x$ increases $y$ by $2$. Starting from $(1,3)$ gives $y=1$ at $x=0$, then $y=5,7,9$ at $x=2,3,4$.\n\nThe completed $y$-row is $1,3,5,7,9$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p2-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the equation of the line.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=2x+1$",
          "worked": "The table gives the $y$-intercept $1$, and the gradient is $2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=mx+c\\\\y&=2x+1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
